🚽 Test case: #197 -- chaining `.` through a pointer-typed field whose
🚽 pointer is still NULL (`next` never assigned) is a clean runtime error,
🚽 not a crash. Written as an assignment target (no yapping) so the error
🚽 is the program's only output, mirroring struct_pointer_null_deref_fail
🚽 (#196's variable-base equivalent).
gang Node {
    rizz val;
    gang Node *next;
};

skibidi main {
    gang Node n;
    n.val = 3;
    n.next.val = 5;
}
